WHAT THIS COVERS
----------------
The LLM-generated annotations produced for "Reliable but Sensitive: Evaluating
LLM Annotation Beyond Performance", and the files derived from them:

  data_work/raw/**          model label files, one directory per model
  data_work/processed/**    the unified long/aggregated analysis datasets,
                            except kern_full.csv (see Third-party material)
  data_work/outputs/**      derived tables and coefficient exports
  plots/**                  derived figures

You are free to share and adapt this material for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the license, and
indicate if changes were made.

  License text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
  Summary:      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Suggested attribution:

  LLM annotation data from "Reliable but Sensitive: Evaluating LLM Annotation
  Beyond Performance" (2026), CC BY 4.0.

THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
--------------------
1. Tweet text (the `tweet` column of data_work/processed/df_agg.csv and the
   corresponding column of the raw label files).

   These tweets come from the Davidson et al. (2017) hate-speech and offensive
   language corpus, reaching this repository through the subsample annotated by
   Kern et al. (2023):

     https://github.com/t-davidson/hate-speech-and-offensive-language

   That corpus is distributed under the MIT License, reproduced below, which
   permits redistribution. Screen names have been masked and URLs removed in
   the copies here. Copyright in the tweets themselves rests with their
   authors, not with Davidson et al., and redistribution of tweet text (as
   opposed to tweet IDs) may also be constrained by the platform's developer
   terms; neither is altered by the MIT grant or by this file.

   Cite the corpus as:

     Davidson, T., Warmsley, D., Macy, M., & Weber, I. (2017). Automated Hate
     Speech Detection and the Problem of Offensive Language. Proceedings of the
     11th International AAAI Conference on Web and Social Media (ICWSM '17),
     512-515.

